  "body": "A form control is disabled if either it has a \"disabled\" attribute or it's in a fieldset that does.\r\n\r\n`.disabled` reflects the attribute, but there's no sane way to find the fieldset state without doing annoying tree-walking.\r\n\r\nWe should consider having a getter that directly exposes the disabled state of the control.  I just saw someone asking for that today...",
